      "id": "4r80pxf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Classification of Rivers of India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Indian river systems are broadly categorized into Himalayan and Peninsular rivers.",
        "The Himalayan system comprises major rivers such as the Ganga, Indus, and Brahmaputra along with their tributaries.",
        "Peninsular rivers are differentiated by direction into East Flowing and West Flowing systems.",
        "Geological structures and terrain determine specific drainage patterns across Indian landscapes.",
        "Important dams and river projects serve multiple purposes including hydroelectric power and irrigation."
      ],
      "id": "7uwx2dq"
    },
